Q: Printing Page number when printing html A: <p>I use the following approach to add page number and total number of pages, e.g. &quot;2/10&quot;, when printing (and removing the page number from the 1st/cover-page):</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@page {

    /*
     * Add page numbers to the bottom of each page 
     */

    @bottom-center {
        content: counter(page) &quot;/&quot; counter(pages);
        color: #c0c0c0;
    }
}

@page :first {

    /*
     * Remove page numbers from cover-page
     */

    @bottom-center {
        content: &quot;&quot;;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The approach was inspired by: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/60857567/8229998">https://stackoverflow.com/a/60857567/8229998</a></p>

Q: XPages, how to validate the number of entries in a multi-value field/control? A: <p>You can do it with a CustomValidator routine.</p>
<p>xml</p>
<pre><code>&lt;asp:CustomValidator ID=&quot;ListBox5ItemsValidator&quot; runat=&quot;server&quot;
    OnServerValidate=&quot;ListBox5ItemsValidator_ServerValidate&quot;
    ClientValidationFunction=&quot;ListBox5ItemsValidator_ClientValidate&quot;
    ControlToValidate=&quot;MyListBox&quot;&gt;
&lt;/asp:CustomValidator&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Server-side code:</p>
<p>csharp</p>
<pre><code>protected void ListBox5ItemsValidator_ServerValidate(
        object source, ServerValidateEventArgs args) {

    int selectionCount = 0;
    foreach (ListItem item in MyListBox.Items) {
        if (item.Selected) selectionCount++;
    }
    args.IsValid = (selectionCount &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; selectionCount &lt;= 5);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Client-side code:</p>
<p>javascript</p>
<pre><code>function ListBox5ItemsValidator_ClientValidate(sender, args) {
    var selectionCount = $('#&lt;% =MyListBox.ClientID %&gt; option:selected').length;
    args.IsValid = (selectionCount &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; selectionCount &lt;= 5);
};
</code></pre>
<p>Replace MyListBox with the actual name of your ListBox...</p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/4187176">https://stackoverflow.com/a/4187176</a></p>

Q: Tailwind CSS generates incorrect compiled CSS for escaped characters of JavaScript strings A: <p>Since TailwindCSS does not execute the code and does not evaluate how many backslashes will appear in the final output, it can only rely on the class name as written in the source. Therefore, you must ensure that the correct class name appears in the JSX code, and to achieve this you need to use <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/raw" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>String.raw()</code></a> to avoid forcing the backslash to be escaped as a string literal:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>String.raw`after:content-['\a0_·_']` // will be &quot;after:content-['\a0_·_']&quot;
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div className={String.raw`after:content-['\a0_·_']`}/&gt;{/* class=&quot;after:content-['\a0_·_']&quot; */}
</code></pre>
